cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Severity of Powered Personal Transporter (E-Scooter) Casualties in Great Britain, 2021-2025: A Comparative Analysis with Pedal Cyclists and Motorcyclists Using STATS19 Data"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-21"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived data for a comparative study of e-scooter casualty
  severity in Great Britain, using UK STATS19 road safety open data with pedal
  cyclists and motorcyclists as comparison groups. E-scooter casualties had 1.59
  times the adjusted odds of being killed or seriously injured compared with pedal
  cyclists (95% CI 1.49-1.69), and the estimate was robust to correction for a
  mid-series change in severity-recording practice.
keywords:
  - e-scooter
  - micromobility
  - road safety
  - injury severity
  - powered personal transporter
  - STATS19
  - transportation engineering
